      "content": "I'll read both the original test and the CUT source to understand the code before improving it.Now I understand the test. It verifies that `escapeCssIdentifier` correctly escapes a backspace character (`\\b`, U+0008) within a string — control characters in range U+0001–U+001F are escaped as CSS code points. Let me write an improved, more understandable version.The improved test compiled successfully. The refactored test replaces the cryptic auto-generated name and opaque string literal with a descriptive method name and comments explaining that `\\b` (U+0008, backspace) is a control character in the CSS-escapable range U+0001–U+001F, and that `escapeCssIdentifier` serializes it as the CSS code point escape `\\8 `."
